      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The maximum recommended metformin dose is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for most extended-release products.\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg is well above the usual maximum of 850\u20131,000 mg per dose.\n- **Risk:** An overdose of this size raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nPossible intended orders include:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 500 mg or 850 mg PO two or three times daily, if you're starting or titrating\n- 1700 mg as the *total daily* dose, for example 850 mg twice daily\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily as written, tell me that explicitly and give the clinical rationale. I'd still recommend pharmacy review first."
      }
